The species reference the app serves is derived from public data. Every page
names the source of each figure and photograph, with its licence:

  GBIF Backbone Taxonomy                          CC BY 4.0
  GBIF occurrence records                         CC0 or CC BY per record, as published;
                                                  CC BY-NC records are read for derived
                                                  figures (the map marker, the habitat
                                                  climate) and never published
  World Checklist of Vascular Plants, RBG Kew     CC BY 4.0
  CHELSA V2.1 climatologies                       CC0 1.0
  ETOPO 2022, NOAA NCEI (elevation, land)         public domain (US Government)
  NASA POWER (daily temperatures)                 public domain (US Government)
  Natural Earth coastlines, and its states and    public domain
    provinces, from which the regions' shapes
    are made
  Wikidata (identifiers, article titles, English  CC0 1.0
    names for pages without a GBIF key, the
    list of botanic gardens, arboreta,
    herbaria and zoos)
  iNaturalist and GBIF photographs                CC0, public domain, CC BY, CC BY-SA per photo
  Wikimedia Commons photographs                   CC0, public domain, CC BY, CC BY-SA per file
  Wikipedia summaries                             CC BY-SA 4.0
  OpenAlex (papers listed on pages built          CC0 1.0
    before October 2026)

Read, and published only as codes, names or links: the level-3 region codes
and names of TDWG's World Geographical Scheme for Recording Plant
Distributions, 2nd edition, and its tables that place states and provinces in
regions (github.com/tdwg/wgsrpd; TDWG's own boundary polygons are not used);
IPNI and POWO identifiers (RBG Kew); iNaturalist taxon identifiers; and the
titles and descriptions of GBIF's datasets, read to tell living collections
from genebanks when the species list was made.

The frost watch, which is no part of the reference, shows forecasts asked for
your site: from MET Norway (api.met.no; CC BY 4.0) and, in the
US and its territories, from the National Weather Service (public domain).

The licences' texts:
  CC BY 4.0      https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  CC BY-SA 4.0   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
  CC0 1.0        https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

No other data is used. Nothing about a species is written for its page by a
person or a language model, apart from credited quotations; the templates its
sentences are filled into were written once, the same for every species. See
/about/how in the running app ("Who writes the words").
